WEBVTT

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.489
Open the intended record and verify its identity before making a correction.

00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:09.630
This Training example is Finalized, with record number T R N, twenty

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:15.829
twenty-six, zero zero zero two, and draft reference D, Y X S nine three.

00:00:16.229 --> 00:00:20.520
Its Course entry ends with the code Academy, R E C, twenty-nine.

00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:24.290
Read the recorded author, group and narrative as well.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.780
This is explicitly a fictional software exercise.

00:00:28.299 --> 00:00:31.110
Once you have confirmed the intended record and your authority

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.270
to correct it, choose Amend.

00:00:33.519 --> 00:00:38.030
The editor identifies the same Training record and displays an important notice:

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.059
an amendment is in progress, and the last finalized revision remains authoritative

00:00:43.099 --> 00:00:44.969
until the amendment is finalized.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:47.370
Read that distinction before editing.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:53.940
Station slash group, External ID, dates, Course, Course code, Location

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.519
and Narrative are shown here.

00:00:56.009 --> 00:01:00.419
Opening this editor has not, by itself, replaced the finalized version

00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:02.069
with a newly signed correction.

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:04.640
Edit only the field that needs correction.

00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:10.169
Here, Course code changes from Academy, R E C, twenty-nine, to

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.920
Academy, R E C, twenty-nine A.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:18.149
The Course title, fictional workspace and software-only narrative remain unchanged.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:22.209
A focused correction is easier to review later than an unexplained

00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:24.219
rewrite of unrelated details.

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:27.670
Check the new field value and the amendment notice before

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.199
moving to the save controls.

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:33.350
At the bottom of the editor, review Reason code, Reason and

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.939
the available save actions.

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:38.439
This example uses Training Correction as its reason code.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:40.899
The attestation is still unchecked.

00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:45.419
Choose Save draft to retain the working correction without finalizing it.

00:01:45.849 --> 00:01:48.140
Save and finalize is a separate action.

00:01:48.489 --> 00:01:52.689
The complete reason and attestation will be reviewed again in the finalization

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:54.730
panel before the amendment is signed.

00:01:55.019 --> 00:01:58.269
The reopened record shows the corrected Course entry ending

00:01:58.269 --> 00:02:02.289
in twenty-nine A, while the amendment-in-progress notice remains.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:06.020
Its existing Finalized badge does not remove that warning.

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:10.569
Read the two together: a saved working correction and the authoritative

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:12.599
finalized revision are distinct.

00:02:13.029 --> 00:02:17.619
Edit and Abandon amendment are available above, and the separate Finalize panel

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:19.750
asks for a reason and attestation.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.070
This example continues with the intended correction rather than abandoning it.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:29.120
In Finalize, the reason code is Training Correction and the full Reason says,

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.430
Correct fictional course code only.

00:02:31.899 --> 00:02:36.080
Read the attestation before selecting it: the record must be accurate and

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.920
complete to the best of your knowledge.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:42.930
This recorded attestation concerns the explicitly fictional software record, with

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.299
no physical training or response claimed.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.729
Once the correction, reason and attestation are appropriate, choose

00:02:49.729 --> 00:02:51.740
Finalize to complete this amendment.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:55.629
After finalization, the reopened record is marked Amended.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:59.350
The record number and draft reference are retained, and the Course

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.650
entry still ends in twenty-nine A.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.930
Verify this actual returned state rather than assuming that an earlier

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.779
draft save completed the amendment.

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:11.710
Keeping the record's identity while retaining its revision history makes

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.950
a correction easier for another authorized reviewer to follow.

00:03:15.149 --> 00:03:17.860
In History, read the numbered transitions.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.639
Revision two is Amended with the Training Correction reason code; revision

00:03:22.639 --> 00:03:24.649
one remains Finalized beneath it.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.460
The rows identify the actor and date.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.790
Use Compare with previous on the amended row to review what changed

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.730
between those two saved versions.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.669
Verify the intended row before choosing the comparison action.

00:03:37.899 --> 00:03:43.129
Revision comparison explicitly says Revision one compared with revision two.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:47.140
Read Field, Before and After across the same row.

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:52.260
Details dot Course Code changes from Academy, R E C, twenty-nine,

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:54.680
to the version ending twenty-nine A.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:58.350
This comparison shows one changed field for this correction.

00:03:58.729 --> 00:04:02.190
Compare the actual values with the stated reason before drawing

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.889
a conclusion about the amendment.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:09.350
This walkthrough is reading the comparison page; it does not perform a PDF export.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:13.590
Return to the record and find revision two's Amended row in History.

00:04:14.039 --> 00:04:17.300
Choose View on that row to inspect its saved content.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.709
This is a different question from the comparison: the comparison identifies

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:26.499
differences, while View opens the selected revision's complete rendered record.

00:04:26.849 --> 00:04:30.229
Keep the row number and transition together so you open the version

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:32.140
you actually intend to inspect.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.919
The opened page identifies the department, record number and revision two.

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:42.189
Under Details, Course Code contains the corrected value ending twenty-nine A.

00:04:42.559 --> 00:04:46.510
The fictional location and truthful software-only narrative are retained.

00:04:46.969 --> 00:04:51.289
Attachments lists the recorded file metadata, including the exercise handout.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:55.649
Read the revision heading before treating a saved page as the current version

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.680
or comparing it with another copy.

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.629
Return to History again and find revision one's Finalized row.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.180
Choose View on that original row.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.560
The presence of an amended revision above it has not removed this earlier

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.190
saved version from the history.

00:05:10.579 --> 00:05:14.590
Selecting the correct row lets an authorized reviewer inspect the original

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:16.989
content alongside the later correction.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:21.650
The original page identifies revision one and retains the earlier Course Code

00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:24.159
ending twenty-nine, without the added A.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.809
Its software-exercise narrative and attachment metadata are still present.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.840
Reading both saved versions and their comparison makes the correction

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:37.429
traceable: you can identify the original value, the amended value and

00:05:37.429 --> 00:05:41.400
the stated correction reason without rewriting the earlier saved snapshot.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.399
The same careful correction and revision checks can support authorized

00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:49.569
documentation in community paramedicine or mental health response teams,

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:54.429
search-and-rescue organizations, security companies, wildland contractors

00:05:54.429 --> 00:05:58.669
and industrial emergency teams, as well as Fire and EMS departments.

00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:02.909
Use a specific reason, keep the attestation truthful and

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:04.440
inspect the saved result.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:10.309
A working draft, a finalized amendment, a comparison and an earlier revision each

00:06:10.309 --> 00:06:14.629
serve a different purpose when explaining what a record said and how it changed.
